			</font>
          </td>
        </tr>
		
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top">
            <hr>
            <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Tuesday, 
            February&nbsp; 17&nbsp; 2004&nbsp;&nbsp;<font size=1><i>- posted by&nbsp;Veer</i></font><br>
            </font> 
            <hr>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="4" color="#333333">The Battles of Sol Ro Tower</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333333" size="2">
            <table border="0" width="700">
<tr>
<td>
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">

<p>Yester eve, the Minions gathered at the site overlooking the entryway to tranquility just as they always do. The scouts were sent out into the planes of the gods to see what fruit was ripe for the picking. As always, there was much discussion by the Baars... Which target would be picked? Which god would fall this night? Although some may have forseen the inevitable, many were taken by joyful surprise when it was announced that the time to enter the Sol Ro Tower had come.

<p>Preparing for the battle was painstaking. Despite weeks of time and effort well spent, not all had earned the right to go. Thankfully, the strength of those who had earned the right was great enough that a few of those who did not were also able to join in.

<p>Thus the epic begins. Let it be known that Jiva and Rizlona were the first to fall. Let it be known that the others will soon follow. Let it be known that the Minions have placed their mark upon the towers. And let Sol Ro tremble...

</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>
<center>
<table border="1" width="700" cellpadding="10" bordercolor="#000000">
<tr><td align="center">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1513.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#3333FF">
MoKB vs Jiva</font><br /><br />
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1514.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#3333FF">
MoKB vs Rizlona</font>
</td>
<td>
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
<h3>Invictus</h3>

<p>Out of the night that covers me,
<br>. . . Black as the Pit from pole to pole,
<br>I thank whatever gods may be
<br>. . . For my unconquerable soul.

<p>In the fell clutch of circumstance
<br>. . . I have not winced nor cried aloud,
<br>Under the bludgeonings of chance
<br>. . . My head is bloody, but unbowed.

<p>Beyond this place of wrath and tears
<br>. . . Looms but the horror of the shade,
<br>And yet the menace of the years
<br>. . . Finds, and shall find me, unafraid.

<p>It matters not how strait the gate,
<br>. . . How charged with punishments the scroll,
<br>I am the master of my fate:
<br>. . . I am the captain of my soul.

<p>----- William Ernest Henley

</td>
</tr>
</table>
</center>

</font>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
			
			</font>
          </td>
        </tr>
		
