            <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Thursday, 
            February&nbsp; 5&nbsp; 2004&nbsp;&nbsp;<font size=1><i>- posted by&nbsp;Conqueso</i></font><br>
            </font> 
            <hr>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="4" color="#333333">A Get Well Note to Otwyna from MoKB</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333333" size="2">
            <table border="0" width="700">
<tr><td align="center">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1500.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#333333">
MoKB Celebrity Guest: Pikkanchu</font>
</td>
<td><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
All of MoKB wishes Otwyna a speedy recovery. We are all rooting for you.

We tried to think of different ways to cheer you up, and we considered hiring a celebrity. Due to a massive touring schedule, Nonsync was not available. Blazingmoon tried to write a special note to Otwyna for us, but it only read "Tge Welq Sono". Strag was always getting "smushed" anytime he tried to deliver our "get well" gift so we tried to do the next best thing. Although he is a little "animated", we asked Pikkanchu to come and try to put a smile on Otwyna's face. Get well soon Otwyna. We all miss you.
</font>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
			
			</font>
          </td>
        </tr>
		
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top">
            <hr>
            <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Tuesday, 
            January&nbsp; 13&nbsp; 2004&nbsp;&nbsp;<font size=1><i>- posted by&nbsp;Hyrin</i></font><br>
            </font> 
            <hr>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="4" color="#333333">Mithaniel Marr - Dead</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333333" size="2">
            <table border="0" width="700">
<tr><td align="center">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1486.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#333333">
Show me a mirror!</font>
</td>
<td><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
With an ego matched only by Christian Bale in American Psycho, Macho Man, uh Mistmore, uh Mithaniel Marr, has to 

be the most self righteous ex-deity in Norrath. I swear if there were mirrors in EverQuest, HoHb 

would be covered in them. Mithaniel cannot get enough of himself. Every single wall has his face 

plastered on it, and every alcove or empty space has a statue of him. I dare not ponder what his 

bedroom looks like, and as to why Tunare is so snobbish I won’t even go there.</font>
</td>
</tr>

<tr><td colspan="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
Either way this fruit’s reign is over. Last night we zoned into HoHb for the first time as a guild. 

I tell you though trying to just run there when you have a bunch of people needing to be flag 

dragged is a really bad idea! Having a bunch of people standing at the HoHb zone line next to a 

bunch of KOS mobs with invis dropping one by one is not fun! Doing a corpse recovery on top of a 

bunch of KOS mobs however is fun! That was quite the adrenaline rush!<br /><br />

Anyway, we eventually got everyone we could into HoHb and started beating stuff up. Gosh, this zone 

is easy I thought. INC, mobs dead. INC mobs dead. Opps respawn, 4 mobs in camp, mobs dead. Named 

inc, Strag dead *laugh*, named dead. We get up to Mithaniel. Re-clear the room, pull him. Kill him. 

Wow that was easy.</font>
</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2" align="center">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1487.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#333333">
Mithaniel Marr is Gobsmacked</font>
<br /><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Welcome to The Tower of 

Solusek Ro.</font>
</td></tr>
</table>


			
			</font>
          </td>
        </tr>
		
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top">
            <hr>
            <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Tuesday, 
            January&nbsp; 6&nbsp; 2004&nbsp;&nbsp;<font size=1><i>- posted by&nbsp;Hyrin</i></font><br>
            </font> 
            <hr>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="4" color="#333333">Bertoxxulous Dead</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333333" size="2">
            <table width="700">
<tr><td align="center">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1466.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#333333">
Bertoxxulous dead at the hands of MOKB</font>
</td></tr>

<tr><td><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
The first time we entered CoDb we only had an inkling of how the Bert raid went. We valiently went forward tho. And we died, tho we did get to actually see Bert. We gamely tried again tho and failed again and slowly learned. Then last night we smacked down Carprin and decided to once again face Bertox. We went in and things went flawlessly. Thanks to a great guild, good listening, tons of co-operation and innumerable monk deaths we slew the ugliest of the gods with time to spare. It was a fabulous night and there was much rejoicing.<br /><br />- Otwyna</font>
</td></tr></table>
			
			</font>
          </td>
        </tr>
		

